verses.tf_en:
① **«وَالَّذِیْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَاتَّبَعَتْهُمْ ذُرِّیَّتُهُمْ بِاِیْمَانٍ اَلْحَقْنَا بِهِمْ ذُرِّیَّتَهُمْ»** (And those who accepted faith, and whose descendants followed them with faith – We have joined their descendants with them,) — A monumental theological manifestation of divine bounty (*Ilhaq adh-Dhurriyyah*): Those who embraced true faith, whose progeny also followed them upon the path of faith, Allah Almighty shall, through His boundless grace, elevate those children to the exalted heavenly stations of their righteous parents, reuniting the families so that the parents' eyes may be completely delighted, even if the personal deeds of the descendants were lesser in merit;
② **«وَمَاۤ اَلَتْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ عَمَلِهِمْ مِّنْ شَیْءٍ»** (And have not reduced anything for them from their deeds;) — And We shall not deduct or diminish the slightest fraction from the earned reward and elevated rank of the parents in order to bestow it upon the children; rather, Allah elevates the children purely out of His infinite celestial generosity;
③ **«كُلُّ امْرِئٍۭ بِمَا كَسَبَ رَهِینٌۭ»** (Every soul is trapped in its own deeds) — Every individual is held collateral and accountable for their own deeds: The disbelievers and unrepentant sinners remain imprisoned by the burden of their misdeeds, whereas the believers are emancipated and honored through faith and divine mercy.
